        "faq_MnVPkd": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "faq_que": "Do I Need to Use a Rack Fan?",
            "faq_ans": "<p>While rack fans do help extend the life and performance of your equipment, if you are using an open rack in a temperature controlled environment, there is no need for rack fans. <a href=\"/blogs/articles/5-things-to-consider-when-purchasing-a-rack-system\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"5 Things to Consider When Purchasing a Rack System\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p><p>Thermal management should not be taken lightly, the components in these racks create a lot of heat and need to be kept cool by rack fans. <a href=\"/blogs/how-to/how-to-prepare-for-your-rack-installation\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"How to Prepare for Your Rack Installation\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p>"
          }
        }
      },
